# Offline CP2K twin note — dos-metallic-si

Not an absolute-energy / absolute-DOS twin of Atomiverse ONCV-PW.
Documents the Quickstep product counterpart of metallic-occupation DOS.

## Intent

- Geometry: diamond Si, a = 5.43 Å, 2-atom fcc primitive (same as
  `si_bands_dos_note.inp` / `reg_bands-dos-si`).
- SCF: PADE, GTH-PADE-q4 + DZVP-GTH-q4, MP 2×2×2.
- Metallic occupations: `&SMEAR METHOD FERMI_DIRAC` with
  \(k_B T \approx 0.02\) Ry (≈ 3158 K), `ADDED_MOS` ≥ 4.
- Post-SCF: denser k-mesh eigenvalues / DOS print for offline inspection
  of \(E_F\) and occupied state count ≈ 8 electrons/cell.

## Suggested CP2K input skeleton

```
&GLOBAL
  PROJECT si_dos_metallic
  RUN_TYPE ENERGY
&END GLOBAL
&FORCE_EVAL
  METHOD Quickstep
  &DFT
    &QS
      EPS_DEFAULT 1.0E-10
    &END QS
    &MGRID
      CUTOFF 300
      REL_CUTOFF 60
    &END MGRID
    &SCF
      SCF_GUESS ATOMIC
      EPS_SCF 1.0E-6
      MAX_SCF 50
      ADDED_MOS 4
      &SMEAR
        METHOD FERMI_DIRAC
        ELECTRONIC_TEMPERATURE [K] 3157.75
      &END SMEAR
      &DIAGONALIZATION
        ALGORITHM STANDARD
      &END DIAGONALIZATION
      &MIXING
        METHOD BROYDEN_MIXING
        ALPHA 0.4
      &END MIXING
    &END SCF
    &XC
      &XC_FUNCTIONAL PADE
      &END XC_FUNCTIONAL
    &END XC
    &KPOINTS
      SCHEME MONKHORST-PACK 2 2 2
    &END KPOINTS
  &END DFT
  &SUBSYS
    &CELL
      A 0.0 2.715 2.715
      B 2.715 0.0 2.715
      C 2.715 2.715 0.0
      PERIODIC XYZ
    &END CELL
    &COORD
      Si 0.0 0.0 0.0
      Si 1.3575 1.3575 1.3575
    &END COORD
    &KIND Si
      BASIS_SET DZVP-GTH-q4
      POTENTIAL GTH-PADE-q4
    &END KIND
  &END SUBSYS
&END FORCE_EVAL
```

## Pin policy

Record CP2K version, wall, and qualitative \(E_F\) / electron count in
`regressions/pw/dos-metallic-si/REFERENCE.md` when a binary is available.
Never launch CP2K from ctest.
